```

When using cURL to connect over a Unix socket, the hostname is not important. The previous
examples use `localhost`, but any hostname would work.

**Important:** The previous examples assume you're using cURL 7.50.0 or above. Older versions of cURL used a [non-standard URL notation](https://github.com/moby/moby/issues/17960) when using a socket connection. If you're' using an older version of cURL, use `http:/<API version>/` instead, for example: `http:/v{{% param "latest_engine_api_version" %}}/containers/1c6594faf5/start`.

{{< /tab >}}
{{< /tabs >}}

